This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is shard 'b' of enforcement-map-derivations, and it inherits that fixture's reason
without qualification: the subject is scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh, which is not
shipped to consumers. A fixture whose subject is absent cannot run. It is permanently
dormant, and a dormant fixture in the consumer's suite is worse than no fixture, because
the catalog then claims the check is self-tested when nothing tests it there.

A SHARD INHERITS ITS SIBLING'S MARKER BY CARRYING ITS OWN, NOT BY POINTING AT IT. The
exemption is DERIVED per directory — I8, I74, install.sh and preclassify.sh's map_consumer()
each read the marker beside the fixture — so a shard without one is shippable by every
reader that matters, and would land in a consumer as a directory whose subject is not there.
That is the exact failure the parent's marker was written after, and adding a directory is
precisely when it can happen again.
